cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EdgeFDL in research or engineering reports, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "EdgeFDL: Edge-network Fault Detection and Localization"
abstract: >-
  EdgeFDL locates faulty links in edge networks (campus, branch and factory networks) from the
  network-management server, read-only towards the devices and without production fault data.
  For each network it builds an equivalent virtual network (an analytic simulator, Linux network
  namespaces with FRR OSPF and tc, or LXD containers), enumerates the fault space, generates
  trigger-aligned and domain-randomized samples, and trains a small Double/Dueling DQN agent with a
  link-shared encoder and an active deep-probe action. Online, it measures the network every 5
  seconds with light probes, and when an anomaly persists it raises one alarm per fault that names
  the link and the fault type (link down, delay, loss, jitter, bandwidth degradation, route drift),
  with evidence, vendor-specific troubleshooting commands and remediation actions rehearsed on the
  virtual network. Alarms are exported through a Web dashboard, a REST API, Syslog, Webhook,
  Prometheus metrics and CSV logs.
authors:
